{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun","id":1100320,"title":"What Makes this game Fun?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-04T20:37:59-07:00","id":1100320,"title":"What Makes this game Fun?","content":"welp, i cant help but ask random strangers this. as my group is causing me a bigger headache then the world has aspirin. as they seem to imply that this game is not intended to be fun in any way. just a sad slog threw the sad sad existence of being a vampire. or worse trying to meta game in a way to screw over other players. and this only leaves me scratching my head as i wonder what exactly i am doing hear.<br /> <br /> so i will ask this, coming from a guy who only really played the old video game. what exactly am i doing wrong? because i heard everything from deal with it to this is a game for only a small nitch of people. when i thought this was a game about being a bad ass vampire, meeting all sorts of characters, dealing with political intrigue and generally just having a good time as i roll some dice. so was i wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13272-rman88","name":"rman88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T20:56:11-07:00","id":1100325,"title":"","content":"I think the video game your referring to was Masquerade, not requiem. Maybe. Either way.<br /> <br /> Vampire is a game about backstabbing - but, like many games, only if you make it such. Think game-of-thrones and you've got yourself a vampire game - except instead of playing mortal people in a strange, hostile world, you are playing a secret collection of people with the power to control others with their very blood, monsters who prey on the weak by their very nature. You are playing a creature that was once a human, and has to come to terms with the fact that it is not - and is now a part of a community of sharks who make eternity interesting by playing russian roulette with lives.<br /> <br /> So... Pretty much its a game about playing a bad assed vampire, meeting all sorts of characters, dealing with political intrigue and generally having a good time as you roll some dice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There are a lot of styles of play too. You can play a game entirely based around cutthroat politics, but you can also play a game where you span the centuries, all trying to tell a story told over the coarse of millenia.<br /> <br /> That said, if your having an issue with the game, it might not be the game - but the people you are playing with. Because the game itself is a toolkit for people to have fun - it's not a strict regiment that must be played in a way that ostracizes certain players trying to figure the game out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T21:02:03-07:00","id":1100326,"title":"","content":"I don't care much at all for playing the game about undead politics, FWIW.<br /> <br /> For me, Requiem is a game about intense personal drama, about exploring how normal people like you and me react to extraordinary circumstances, and how they either fight tooth and nail to resist their own monstrosity, or tumble down into it despite their best intentions not to. How does someone handled being turned into a creature of violence? How would they cope to the apparent loss of their own soul, and the shift away from being recognizably human? What bizarre coping mechanisms would the dead create to deal with the weight of immortality and their own alien hungers? That's a rich narrative vein that makes for powerful stories, and that's before factoring in metaphors - for addiction, for toxic relationships, for other things - that vampires easily represent. <br /> <br /> So is it &quot;fun&quot; in the same way an action movie or a classic high fantasy adventure game is? No, but I'm not always (in fact, almost never) looking for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T21:05:48-07:00","id":1100328,"title":"","content":"If your group is dead set on interpreting to a narrow definition of &quot;fun&quot; as &quot;being badass and kicking ass,&quot; then frankly no amount of advice from us will persuade them. Think about why people read tragedies and find meaning in them. Think about why the main characters in fiction sometimes fail, instead of being promised of success in everything they do. Requiem is a lot like that.<br /> <br /> Except that this too is still shallow. You <i>can</i> be a badass master of the night, mingling with every manner of people from every sphere in the world, fending off the Prince and his lackeys in a grand political intrigue. It's just that the game firmly reminds you that your actions <i>do</i> have consequences. And the game doesn't <i>force</i> you to avoid those consequences like the plague. You can take them head on, refusing to go down silently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T21:10:47-07:00","id":1100329,"title":"","content":"I mean, I don't honestly think Requiem is mutually incompatible with vampire badassery that doesn't necessarily find much when it delves deep beneath the surface of a character, either. I enjoy it when personal drama and art emerge from the interactions within the game, and I've rolled self-loathing, alienated educated Catholics doomed to a theologically untenable damnation, but I've also rolled opportunistic lunatics hiding behind a thin visage of human sentiment, with &quot;do a fun homicide&quot; on their list of aspirations. The best games meet somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> I'll second Jakondite. It's an important element in any game that you and your players get on the same page with regards to what you want out of a game and what you expect to make it do. If they, say, have a strong vision of what they think Vampire is, and you don't see where the part you were looking forward to comes in, or if it's vice-versa, talk it out and see if you can find where the Venn circles overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T21:13:24-07:00","id":1100332,"title":"","content":"You might be thinking of Masquerade, but if you mean Requiem it's in the introduction.<br /> <br /> 'Vampire is a game of visceral drama and personal horror.<br /> Vampire is about sex and murder, about power and wild defiance. It\u2019s about urban squalor and the romance of the city. It\u2019s about what\u2019s wrong with you \u2014 yes, you \u2014 and how that shapes the monster you\u2019ll become.<br /> Vampire is also about thrilling action and nail-biting paranoia. It\u2019s about dying young and being a great-looking corpse. It\u2019s about acting out in all of the ways we imagine we would, if only we couldn\u2019t see ourselves in the mirror.<br /> Vampire is a game about dead people and it should make you feel alive.<br /> Vampire is built on contrast, taking place in a World of Darkness with blinding whites and pitch blacks. Characters try to stay in the cool, comfortable grays, but they can\u2019t hide all the time. And, hey, they look good in black.'<br /> <br /> Basically, it's about being a monster and having fun with it while still trying to have fun with those human bits you have leftover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-05-2017, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T21:25:33-07:00","id":1100335,"title":"","content":"Well, sure, the core of Requiem is the long slow loss of everything except the few things the PC's will hold onto and thus make eternal-but that's a <i>really</i> long time frame.<br /> <br /> THere's time, in that long, slow sequel, to attend festivals and pageantries. To love and lust and drink deep. To stumble down the street puking up blood because what even the hell was that dude smoking while your friends laugh at you and trudge to pick you up. To watch movies and riff on the twenty foot pretty-boy angsting it up. To play a game of tag across rooftops. To eat a god damned <i>hotdog </i>(that you will subsequently puke up, but hey, you <i>can</i> taste it).<br /> <br /> Requiem is a dark game that deals with inevitability-but that loss loses meaning if you do nothing <i>but </i>lose. Characters will cope, move on, change, justify, twist and turn, and do things as they seek to live with themselves-and it's important to know that they can, will, and should <i>live</i>.<br /> <br /> Live long enough and life loses it's savor, sure. It can become too much of a thing-being a person is hard, after all, and one can only carry so much before something inevitably crumbles-and vampires pick up some of the heaviest shit. But if the vampire of a player reaches that point and finds that they have not managed to hold onto something other than blood-slicked misery, they missed the point. This game is not being dead-this game is dying the long way around, with all the weird, zany, fun, heroic, and sometimes poignant items such a bucket list includes.<br /> <br /> With strange aeons, even death may chuckle at that one stupid joke Fry told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-05-2017, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T22:29:27-07:00","id":1100342,"title":"","content":"There are two main points that define Vampire the Requiem: the aforementioned Requiem, and the Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> The Requiem is the tragic part of Vampire. It's the usually slow, sometimes fast, but always inevitable (or so they say) degradation of the self until all that you were and everything that makes you you fades away until all that's left is the hunger. It's where you get pathos. It's where the character becomes sympathetic and relatable. It's when your character realizes what they're becoming and how they chose to handle it. It's often sad, often tragic, but it's the part that often matters the most. In other words it's the down beats of the story, and gives the character's substance.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Danse Macabre. The part of Vampire that gazes into the abyss and laughs. The part that says &quot;better get this done tonight, because tomorrow may never come.&quot; It's where the fun comes into play. It's what brings life into the Covenants. It's why Kindred get up each night and live the f$&amp;k out of the night until the dawn. It's where vampires make love, war, political intrigue, unearth forbidden secrets, and paint the town red. It's also when they burn, when they're reduced to ash. No slow death in the Game of Princes, you either win or you die for good. These are the up beats of the story, and make the setting itself come to unholy life. <br /> <br /> Hope that helps. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 06-05-2017, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T22:39:16-07:00","id":1100343,"title":"","content":"If you want an example of something high-action that still fits the tone of Requiem, I'd honestly say there's an argument to be made for <i>Hotline Miami</i>; you're out of control, your real life is fading away, and what remains of your existence is meaningless hungry violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T22:52:03-07:00","id":1100345,"title":"","content":"On a less overall-thematic-point that relies on Arc's personal preferences, my two main arguments for what makes this game fun in a more immediate sense-Chapter One of Requiem Second Edition.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sexy, Brutal Appeal of Power, or the Clans-</b> Requiem Second Edition went a long way to make it's character options strange, powerful, and <i>damned sexy</i>. There's a blood-slick style to the lot of them, and it's got a simple elegance to it's power appeal.<br /> <br /> Be the one who controls the eyes as the Daeva, and lace the crowd with murderous intent as you make a few jokes, melt hearts with just a wink, and stand as their deity, stronger and faster and so-all-encompassingly important than they ever will be.<br /> <br /> Howl obscenities at the monsters as the Gangrel-they don't even fucking know you wear all their faces. Run with wolves, choke a soul with the smoke of your corpse, and smile with teeth too wide as the asshole realizes he didn't smash your face in-you'll survive the end of worlds, and ravage anything that thinks otherwise.<br /> <br /> Laugh from the shadows as they miss your Cheshire smile as the Mehket-and then poison them with those nasty little sins they thought were safe. You know every lie anyone's ever told, who they'd hurt the most, who could be saved by the truth, and know that they'll never find you, too busy chasing the voice you play in their head.<br /> <br /> Challenge nightmares to blinking contests and leave them sobbing as the Nosferatu-you're every ghost of vengeance they hoped to leave buried, the blood of maggots squirming out of their closets, their beds, their eyes as you break their minds and bodies, never more than the boogieman in the shadows their parents lied to them about.<br /> <br /> Rule the court and make the idiots dance as the Ventrue-you wear your right to conquer and lead like armor, lead sliding off you like rain, your words infecting beasts simple and evolved, making the rats feast on the cats and the rich and powerful to dress themselves in shit against their will, all in service to your inherent right to reign.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sweet Joy of Transgression, or the Covenants-</b> You're not human, and sure-humanity has a lot of important things you should try to hold on to.There's a richness to their life that you might appreciate more now that you're dead. But let's be honest-there's a thrill to breaking the taboos. You're not human, so why should you be <i>wholly</i> bound to them?<br /> <br /> There are swine in the towers, and the Carthian Revolution is going to rip them from their leather-wrapped chairs and toss them out the windows. Set the world on fire and build brave new worlds in the ashes, Your were so powerless against whatever the ruling class was before, but now? Now you can unmake them with everything that empowers them.<br /> <br /> Those fuckers who keep trying to upstage you? Fuck them! The Invictus not only implores you to kick those parasites in the face, but <i>rewards you</i> for it. And if the idiot above you isn't gripping the ladder tightly enough? Well, if you can rip them off, there's a spot open for you friend. Let them try and climb back up-you know where they hide their bodies.<br /> <br /> There's always some fucks who can't abide, who go too far, who make you and yours look tame-except not, cause you're God's Monster in the Lancea Et Sanctum, and you can call down his unholy wrath to punish the assholes who violate the boundaries, who dare to tread upon your sacred path. Justice is mine, sayeth the chorus of teeth.<br /> <br /> Dance and hunt and fuck and kill with the Circle of the Crone and live the life of the monster in ecstasy and abandon, your life more beautiful and vibrant now that you've let go. Dive into the trance of living, commune with gods, and come back knowing that you are one of them.<br /> <br /> Fuck Nature and Fuck God-The Ordo Dracul knows there's more in this world than curses and bloodlust, and they'll dive into the darkest, most eldritch places to turn themselves inside out, ripping the weakness out of them and returning, transcendent in their actualization of &quot;Whatever doesn't kill you makes you stranger&quot;.<br /> <br /> Combine those two with a human element, of finding ways to connect to the simple, important things that make being human worth it, and you have a recipe for a fun time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T03:14:30-07:00","id":1100385,"title":"","content":"ehh i think your focusing on the bad ass vampire comment a little bit to much. as to be honest i don't feel like regardless of how you play it. you still wont feel like your in power or are super powered. and to be honest my character i had in mind, really did not play the that role. then again my gripe tended to be more of a mechanical one.<br /> <br /> you see, i did not at first worry about this. but before we began the new game. another fellow player kept bringing up issues. issues that he had with the game. and i guess you could say it rube off on me. as it is not really the concept of the core themes of the game that i dislike. nore do i feel like each game much be an action pack romp threw darkness. i guess i should point them out.<br /> <br /> first and foremost is the augment of what a mortal is. the book pretty much states on page 75 that it is a human. thou kindred sometimes refer to anyone who is not one of them as mortal. for me this makes sense to degree as cretin merits would be insanely broken if you could use it on other supernaturals. one bite and you managed to enslave a seer or Gentry to your will. you cannot tell me that isn't broken from a mechanic standpoint? (note i am referring to kiss of the succubus merit)<br /> <br /> another issue that was brought up is morality. for me morality should be more or less a grey area. where context is key to determine if you take a breaking point. for example, why is killing a mass murderer the same breaking point as killing a saint? why is killing someone who ruined your life the same breaking point as killing your best friend? why is killing someone who is guilty of many crimes the same as killing someone who is innocent? it just feels to black and white for me.<br /> <br /> and the last of my gripes have to be this. using powers on other players to fuck with them. yep when you have an arsenal like dominate and majesty. and a few players who like to exploit combos powers. some even claimed that they can force a domination without giving you a single chance to avoid it. and if you do well your meta gaming. which leads to the frustration of just wanting to play the game without having to worry about which player wants to screw you over. we have enough problems as it is with the npcs wanting to do that.<br /> <br /> for me this is what is causing the conflict. not the concept or themes of the game. but just arguments over the rules and the chaos that comes with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13272-rman88","name":"rman88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T03:38:02-07:00","id":1100389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">first and foremost is the augment of what a mortal is. the book pretty much states on page 75 that it is a human. thou kindred sometimes refer to anyone who is not one of them as mortal. for me this makes sense to degree as cretin merits would be insanely broken if you could use it on other supernaturals. one bite and you managed to enslave a seer or Gentry to your will. you cannot tell me that isn't broken from a mechanic standpoint? (note i am referring to kiss of the succubus merit)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever heard of what White Room is? Theoretically, in real life anyone with a gun could walk up the the President and shoot him. Now actually <i>try </i>that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> another issue that was brought up is morality. for me morality should be more or less a grey area. where context is key to determine if you take a breaking point. for example, why is killing a mass murderer the same breaking point as killing a saint? why is killing someone who ruined your life the same breaking point as killing your best friend? why is killing someone who is guilty of many crimes the same as killing someone who is innocent? it just feels to black and white for me. </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you're playing Second Edition, not First Edition? First Edition's Morality I admit, but it's been long since Second Edition moved away from that it. Integrity, used by regular humans, track how well you are coping with the outside world. Humanity 2E, used by vampires, tracks how close you are to the human experience and perspective, not how well you are keeping human rights or something. Killing people casually isn't what most humans do, no matter what's the rationale behind it. Hence, it's a Humanity risk<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the last of my gripes have to be this. using powers on other players to fuck with them. yep when you have an arsenal like dominate and majesty. and a few players who like to exploit combos powers. some even claimed that they can force a domination without giving you a single chance to avoid it. and if you do well your meta gaming. which leads to the frustration of just wanting to play the game without having to worry about which player wants to screw you over. we have enough problems as it is with the npcs wanting to do that. </div> </div> </div>That's like saying pencils should be banned from school because anyone can stab someone to death with it. It's not the problem with the game when it's clearly the players who are using it as an excuse to screw other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T03:54:32-07:00","id":1100394,"title":"","content":"I'd love to answer this one. In my 20's I used to scoff &quot;Who plays vampires? All you do is eat people! How fun is that?&quot; It took another (mumble mumble.. cough... cough..) years to be dragged into a vampire game and really enjoy it. For me, it's not vampires, or werewolves.. it's WoD. All of the splats are designed for storytelling, really strong and awesome storytelling. Personal horror, personal revelation and growth. Play it up as adult enjoyment or play it down as a monty power romp. <br /> <br /> So yeah, it's designed for that. Like all tools, it's only as good as the people who wield it. Find a group or attitude or playstyle that works for you. Have fun! Eat people!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T04:25:38-07:00","id":1100401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100342#post1100342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are two main points that define Vampire the Requiem: the aforementioned Requiem, and the Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> The Requiem is the tragic part of Vampire. It's the usually slow, sometimes fast, but always inevitable (or so they say) degradation of the self until all that you were and everything that makes you you fades away until all that's left is the hunger. It's where you get pathos. It's where the character becomes sympathetic and relatable. It's when your character realizes what they're becoming and how they chose to handle it. It's often sad, often tragic, but it's the part that often matters the most. In other words it's the down beats of the story, and gives the character's substance.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Danse Macabre. The part of Vampire that gazes into the abyss and laughs. The part that says &amp;quot;better get this done tonight, because tomorrow may never come.&amp;quot; It's where the fun comes into play. It's what brings life into the Covenants. It's why Kindred get up each night and live the f$&amp;k out of the night until the dawn. It's where vampires make love, war, political intrigue, unearth forbidden secrets, and paint the town red. It's also when they burn, when they're reduced to ash. No slow death in the Game of Princes, you either win or you die for good. These are the up beats of the story, and make the setting itself come to unholy life. <br /> <br /> Hope that helps. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Dance Macabre was synonymous with the Requiem. IIRC, this was even stated so in the eponymous book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T05:55:53-07:00","id":1100414,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of <b>Vampire</b>, really. There are some things that appeal to me but a lot doesn't. I never quite know what to do with it, and I think some of that stems from 'undead politics' being uninteresting.<br /> <br /> However, take a look at what's behind the politics - what's fueling it? Politics are for the <i>monsters</i> - for the Kindred arguing over who gets to suck blood from which night club and no you don't have permission to drink there, only I can. It's a juxtaposition. When you're young and newly embraced you struggle to retain humanity as more and more of it is harder to hold on to. When your friends and family forget about you - when they <i>die</i>, and you keep going - you just don't <i>give </i>a fuck anymore. Your life has been ruined, stolen from you, and I'm sorry but I have to drink blood every night or I stop existing, <i> what do you want from me</i>?<br /> <br /> Covenants are a mask. It's all a play acted out in mimicry of what you were a century ago. It's not about fitting in or 'doing what you have to do.' It's about <i>giving up</i>. You can't win this fight. You've lost already. It's about surrendering to the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire </b>is a game about this descent.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy</b> is about <i>starting</i> there and trying to remember your long lost humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:01:43-07:00","id":1100478,"title":"","content":"There's all sorts of stuff you can do with it. My group has met local Kindred, investigated other supernatural creatures, begun discussing long-term plans to supplant the Proconsul with a high-ranking NPC they like better. They've made friends and allies, fought Strix, attended/participated in arena matches. <br /> <br /> There hasn't been much back-stabbing. There are a lot of secrets, but it's more &quot;what you don't know you can't be Dominated to tell and can't be held against you if it's discovered&quot; as &quot;what you don't know I can use against you.&quot; It's really up to the players. Mine have chosen a sort of middle path - their goals aren't the same, but the initial stages overlap.<br /> <br /> We've had fun, and we haven't done much angsting or brooding. All the characters have been able to show off their awesome abilities. It's also the lowest-combat game my group has ever played - in half a year of weekly sessions, there were only three real combats plus a couple arena combats (one PC versus NPCs using quick and dirty rules) and an assassination.<br /> <br /> We haven't done as much with Touchstones as I'd like, but that's because there's more you can do with the game than we've had time to do it in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10328-bkwrm79","name":"bkwrm79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:42:55-07:00","id":1100498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100401#post1100401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Dance Macabre was synonymous with the Requiem. IIRC, this was even stated so in the eponymous book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It might have been in first edition, but if I'm remembering correctly those terms are used as two separate alagories to describe existence for the Kindred. I even believe the word used was two-step in 2nd Edition Core, to describe the relation of the Requiem and Danse Macabre. <br /> <br /> But that being said...I could be remembering it incorrectly. The Fog of Eternity will do shit like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:47:03-07:00","id":1100500,"title":"","content":"The Requiem is an individual vampire's &quot;life.&quot; The Danse Macabre is the way all of those Requiems play together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:51:21-07:00","id":1100502,"title":"","content":"As for alternate playstyles: playing the game as insomniac misfits getting in over their heads can be a blast. Basically the Guy Ritchie version of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T11:17:34-07:00","id":1100513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ehh i think your focusing on the bad ass vampire comment a little bit to much. as to be honest i don't feel like regardless of how you play it. you still wont feel like your in power or are super powered. and to be honest my character i had in mind, really did not play the that role. then again my gripe tended to be more of a mechanical one.<br /> <br /> you see, i did not at first worry about this. but before we began the new game. another fellow player kept bringing up issues. issues that he had with the game. and i guess you could say it rube off on me. as it is not really the concept of the core themes of the game that i dislike. nore do i feel like each game much be an action pack romp threw darkness. i guess i should point them out.<br /> <br /> first and foremost is the augment of what a mortal is. the book pretty much states on page 75 that it is a human. thou kindred sometimes refer to anyone who is not one of them as mortal. for me this makes sense to degree as cretin merits would be insanely broken if you could use it on other supernaturals. one bite and you managed to enslave a seer or Gentry to your will. you cannot tell me that isn't broken from a mechanic standpoint? (note i am referring to kiss of the succubus merit)</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;what does mortal mean?&quot; question came up in another thread recently... It's weird to me that this is an issue for people. I don't think the writers are thinking about the word &quot;mortal&quot; as a jargon term that specifically means &quot;these four types of beings but not these other two.&quot; The books are written in natural language and expect the reader to use their own judgment in interpreting them. Sometimes mortal is used as a synonym for human to keep the word choice from getting stale, sometimes it's used for its literal meaning, to refer to anything that has a finite lifespan. Sometimes it's used to refer to humans and other things that are basically human like mages, but not things that are explicitly inhuman like werewolves. It's usually pretty clear from context how it's being used, and when in doubt, the group can discuss it and the Storyteller can make a call. For what it's worth, I definitely wouldn't allow Kiss of the Succubus to work on True Fae. Then again, I probably wouldn't be involving True Fae in my vampire games in the first place, or if I did, I would decide ahead of time how different powers interact with them and inform my players of those rulings in session zero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another issue that was brought up is morality. for me morality should be more or less a grey area. where context is key to determine if you take a breaking point. for example, why is killing a mass murderer the same breaking point as killing a saint? why is killing someone who ruined your life the same breaking point as killing your best friend? why is killing someone who is guilty of many crimes the same as killing someone who is innocent? it just feels to black and white for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you hadn't mentioned the Kiss of the Succubus Merit earlier, I would think you were talking about 1st Edition here. Humanity in 2nd Edition is not about morality. At all. It's about how in touch you are with the human experience. Killing someone isn't a Breaking Point because it's immoral, it's a Breaking Point because killing people isn't something most humans do, and when they do it tends to be a pretty traumatic experience. When your vampire kills someone and isn't shaken by it, they face cognitive dissonance and are forced to face their own inhumanity. It doesn't really matter who you kill, because any murder creates that same dissonance between the vampire's experience and the human experience. That's also why things that aren't the least bit immoral, like watching people eat food, or living for a century, are Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the last of my gripes have to be this. using powers on other players to fuck with them. yep when you have an arsenal like dominate and majesty. and a few players who like to exploit combos powers. some even claimed that they can force a domination without giving you a single chance to avoid it. and if you do well your meta gaming. which leads to the frustration of just wanting to play the game without having to worry about which player wants to screw you over. we have enough problems as it is with the npcs wanting to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Player vs. player conflict is not an assumed part of Requiem. It can be part of Requiem, but it can also be part of any other RPG. Some people like PvP in their RPGs, and other people don't, which is why it's important to have a session zero and establish what everyone wants from the game. It sounds like your issue here is stemming from having different play style preferences than the rest of your group, not from the existence of various powers. I would recommend talking with your group openly and honestly, letting them know that it's not fun for you to be working against each other, and you would prefer to play characters who work together against something or someone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for me this is what is causing the conflict. not the concept or themes of the game. but just arguments over the rules and the chaos that comes with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, these aren't problems with Requiem itself, these are problems with your group dynamic. Rules arguments can ruin the fun in any game, that's why the GM is supposed to have final say over interpreting the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T12:04:38-07:00","id":1100523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ehh i think your focusing on the bad ass vampire comment a little bit to much. as to be honest i don't feel like regardless of how you play it. you still wont feel like your in power or are super powered. and to be honest my character i had in mind, really did not play the that role. then again my gripe tended to be more of a mechanical one.<br /> <br /> you see, i did not at first worry about this. but before we began the new game. another fellow player kept bringing up issues. issues that he had with the game. and i guess you could say it rube off on me. as it is not really the concept of the core themes of the game that i dislike. nore do i feel like each game much be an action pack romp threw darkness. i guess i should point them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, Mechanics - I can do that, I'm fairly good with rough general understandings of mechanics. So - here we go. (Edit: Well... this is embarrassing. This actually looks alot like Charlaquins. Oh well - another way of saying the same things probably won't do harm)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">first and foremost is the augment of what a mortal is. the book pretty much states on page 75 that it is a human. thou kindred sometimes refer to anyone who is not one of them as mortal. for me this makes sense to degree as cretin merits would be insanely broken if you could use it on other supernaturals. one bite and you managed to enslave a seer or Gentry to your will. you cannot tell me that isn't broken from a mechanic standpoint? (note i am referring to kiss of the succubus merit)</div> </div> </div> </div>The definition of 'mortal' - at least for the purposes of my game (as I technically cannot speak for the writers, but this is my inference) is usually 'human'. Humans with powers fall under this category What this means is that mage's are a viable option, as are ghouls, kinfolk, and psychics/thaumaturges. Gentry are notably -immortal-, and changelings, werewolves, and other similar creates are abmortal. From the perspective of vampire, mortal means human. While certain groups are certainly vulnerable to things like the kiss (mages) they can also literally choose not to be (spend three mana, remove a condition, etc. Actually, that alone means that mages usually have the advantage, so having something broken for dealing with them is not too bad). Most of the games have material that others might consider insanely broken - and usually that perspective is a result of people not truly understanding the various games, their weaknesses and advantages. As another person said, this is mostly an issue with white room - which, if your fellow players are metagaming and performing pvp, is an -actual issue-. If they are not, however, then it is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another issue that was brought up is morality. for me morality should be more or less a grey area. where context is key to determine if you take a breaking point. for example, why is killing a mass murderer the same breaking point as killing a saint? why is killing someone who ruined your life the same breaking point as killing your best friend? why is killing someone who is guilty of many crimes the same as killing someone who is innocent? it just feels to black and white for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been mentioned before, but in second edition vampiric humanity is not morality. Instead, it's your ability to be human. The issue with killing the person who ruined your life and killing your best friend is that they are both <i>incredibly easy to do</i>. From the perspective of an immortal, witnessing someone else's own mortality puts <i>that much difference</i> between yourself and them. Humanity is your ability to blend, or even think of some aspects of yourself as 'human', rather than monster. A sin against humanity is not a strike against your morals - its a reminder of what you are, and what you aren't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100385#post1100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the last of my gripes have to be this. using powers on other players to fuck with them. yep when you have an arsenal like dominate and majesty. and a few players who like to exploit combos powers. some even claimed that they can force a domination without giving you a single chance to avoid it. and if you do well your meta gaming. which leads to the frustration of just wanting to play the game without having to worry about which player wants to screw you over. we have enough problems as it is with the npcs wanting to do that.<br /> <br /> for me this is what is causing the conflict. not the concept or themes of the game. but just arguments over the rules and the chaos that comes with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a mechanical issue. This is a social contract issue. I play in an online game - pvp is a part of the system because of that so we're used to people who are willing to do such powers on other players - but the social contracts we set up prevent people from forcing another character into situations that make them uncomfortable. The goal of a group is to make things fun for all parties - not just the party utilizing the powers. Metagaming is an example of someone putting themself above the enjoyment of the group.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking however - you cannot dominate a person without a mesmerize roll (dominate 1). If I recall, all the majesty rolls require the same before the later effects can be used (majesty 1). These have a contested roll. The rest are resisted, but not contested (recalling dominate, don't have the book on me to doublecheck majesty). This means that you can spend wp to increase your resistance trait by 2 to make a success for them less likely, but if they have mesmerized you already then no further contest is usually involved unless another power interferes to clash. (Someone remind me, is there a rule saying you can't dominate yourself?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 06-05-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:04:41-07:00","id":1100572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1100523#post1100523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Someone remind me, is there a rule saying you can't dominate yourself?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from common sense, there is the very real limitation of not being able to make eye contact with yourself. The victim needs to be able to have that &quot;look into my eyes&quot; effect happen which rules out mirrors to use on oneself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:10:15-07:00","id":1100576,"title":"","content":"I's an RPG, you do what you want with it. The book says the game is about personal horror, sure but there's no wrong way of using it. I know I've used 1E for a game about going to rescue a PC's ex loved one from Arcadia, traveling to Rome to infiltrate the Vatican and retrieve an elder's torpid body, then going back home to fight off an alliance of an ex PC with two fae and a werewolf trying to take over the city (for various reasons, one of which was to get back the loved one) while a member of VII was trying to cause as many deaths as possible. Second game was about stopping a criminal organization led by Dorjan's Childe, then stopping an Icarian's coup and then an Strix invasion and the return of an ancient Strix on Earth, then finally, racing and fighting Zagreus and his pet werewolf in an attempt to hack part of the God Machine.<br /> <br /> There was also personal drama involved in all of this, but I wanted games of epic proportions and I got them and it went just fine. There was backstabbing in the first game as I successfully led the group to start infighting for a few sessions, culminating in a PC executing another PC. The other game was much more peaceful in that regard. To me, vampires hit the sweet spot between the squishy human and the engine of destruction werewolf, while being ignorant enough of the rest of the occult world that they can be surprised by it. I like them because they can pretty much be used for any story and they're robust enough that they can take a lot of punishment without it making a character unplayable for a long time. That story can be about playing an unlucky everyday person who ends up in an abusive relationship with their sire that they, then, project on their own ghouls, but I tend to prefer the large scale adventure type. It works Simply adjust the detachment rolls and one or two other things to make it go more smoothly.<br /> <br /> I'd say I like to take the more hopeful route than the advertised theme. The PCs are vampires. They're damned and they're going to be stuck in a violent and petty society forever and that existence is going to try and break them, but maybe even then, they can be heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T12:46:35-07:00","id":1101346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun#post1100320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when i thought this was a game about being a bad ass vampire, meeting all sorts of characters, dealing with political intrigue and generally just having a good time as i roll some dice. so was i wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a perfectly ligament way to play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:41:54-07:00","id":1101616,"title":"","content":"Maybe have consequences for the players actions? PvP is a legitimate way to do the game, but doing so with meta game knowledge is not. I tend to have out of game talks with those who meta game\u200b or generally make the game not fun. OOC talks sometimes work very well. <br /> <br /> Or maybe IC punishments? A Vampire game I co-gm for had a player who was using Majesty and blood bounding others against the established law of the coterie. When the other coterie mates found out via the Mekhet players use of Auspex, they tied the poor Daeva up and branded her with fire, a mark that won't heal naturally and will have social consequences in court. <br /> <br /> Problem players that are talked to offline and ignore IC punishments aren't being fun and you might consider just removing the problem players entirely.<br /> <br /> This is a situation that can be remedied, and vampire is a wonderful game. I hope you work things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T10:07:50-07:00","id":1101670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rman88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun#post1100320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">welp, i cant help but ask random strangers this. as my group is causing me a bigger headache then the world has aspirin. as they seem to imply that this game is not intended to be fun in any way. just a sad slog threw the sad sad existence of being a vampire. or worse trying to meta game in a way to screw over other players. and this only leaves me scratching my head as i wonder what exactly i am doing hear.<br /> <br /> so i will ask this, coming from a guy who only really played the old video game. what exactly am i doing wrong? because i heard everything from deal with it to this is a game for only a small nitch of people. when i thought this was a game about being a bad ass vampire, meeting all sorts of characters, dealing with political intrigue and generally just having a good time as i roll some dice. so was i wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The vanilla premise of the game is focused around personal horror. It deals with mature, adult themes (with a supernatural element) and is supposed to be addressed from a mature stand point in order to not come across as offensive. Sure, you've got super powers and an infinite life span; but now you have to eat people, avoid direct sunlight, integrate yourself into a cut throat society where nothing is ever done out of the kindness of one's own heart and have to instantly sever any and all personal attachments to your mortal life so as to avoid exposing yourself and the rest of the vampire community. It's supposed to be a pretty traumatic process in character.<br /> <br /> Making the game more lighthearted is usually the result of shard settings that take place in parallel / alternate environments.<br /> <br /> <br /> For me personally, however, this is exactly what caught my interest in the game to begin with. So many games out there are about being the big, flashy hero who kicks ass and doesn't care about the consequences. But WoD takes a more realistic approach set into the modern world. It also shows that the monsters aren't as mindlessly evil as society portrays them to be. They have their own struggles to cope with and you get to see the world from their side of things; instead of playing the hero that exterminates them without a second thought. It's new and intriguing compared to the scores of medieval / futuristic fantasy games out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-08-2017, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T10:41:48-07:00","id":1101676,"title":"","content":"If its an issue of mental power on PVP why not use the rules of social maneuvering between PC.<br /> <br /> If PC 1 manipulated PC 2 to do something, PC 2 can either <br /> <br /> A) Go with the flow and gain a beat.<br /> <br /> B) Agree to an alternative between PC 2 and PC 1 but PC 1 gets to put a condition on PC 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T13:33:52-07:00","id":1101716,"title":"","content":"The core essence of the game is horror. If you think Vampire is about being a kickass undead blood-drinker then it's not your game, because I consider Vampire to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics. But that\u2019s just me.<br /> <br /> Add a personal touch to the game, use your own hometown, with familiar places and familiar names, use contemporary real world issues like racism, extreme-sided politics, homophobia, and social inequity. Try that and see if you can terrify your players with more than what they usually expect from say... a Call of Cthulhu game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 06-08-2017, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:17:07-07:00","id":1101731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1101716#post1101716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core essence of the game is horror. If you think Vampire is about being a kickass undead blood-drinker then it's not your game, because I consider Vampire to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics. But that\u2019s just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am confuse is the OP asking for &quot;how to make Requiem a game about kicking ass and taking names&quot;? Or the whole issues of crossover + PvP use of mental disciplines + the loose definition of mortal?<br /> <br /> Because if its the former, then its kinda wrong. For all the talk about &quot;being about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing......etc etc&quot; Requiem also has some down right stupid silly awesome things to itself like: Templar knight karate choping mage throats, Ordo members that can be Samuel Heights with just 1 coil, magic in the form of pretentious edgy poetry (Threnodies), Carthian member counterspelling by the power of elective democracy, Invictus knights with gun-kata, Gargoyles that look like digimons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T15:24:52-07:00","id":1101759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1101731#post1101731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am confuse is the OP asking for &quot;how to make Requiem a game about kicking ass and taking names&quot;? Or the whole issues of crossover + PvP use of mental disciplines + the loose definition of mortal?<br /> <br /> Because if its the former, then its kinda wrong. For all the talk about &quot;being about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing......etc etc&quot; Requiem also has some down right stupid silly awesome things to itself like: Templar knight karate choping mage throats, Ordo members that can be Samuel Heights with just 1 coil, magic in the form of pretentious edgy poetry (Threnodies), Carthian member counterspelling by the power of elective democracy, Invictus knights with gun-kata, Gargoyles that look like digimons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ignore the fluff and 100+ books published. Take the core concept of each Covenant (pragmatic undead aristocracy, democratic and utilitarian vampires, bloodthirsty and monstrous pagans, self-righteous Judeo-Christian predators, transcendental order of Draconian undead) now, what can you do with these barebone concepts? Even &quot;elective democracy&quot; can be a shark pit of lethal politics, it doesn't necessarily have to be the feudalism of the Invictus that causes all the horror. Just look at the chaos today's democracy can create.<br /> <br /> And about the Bloodlines and fancy special powers, do with them what you want, though I mostly tend to ignore them, they are unbalanced and unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T16:19:27-07:00","id":1101780,"title":"","content":"Point was that Requiem can be as much of pant-on-the-head awesome-idiotic as it can be serious and exploring the vampire condition. Also, all that stuff i mentioned werent bloodlines disciplines. They came from the covenants books fluff, the gargoyles mechanics and the secret of the covenant/Core 2ed core merits. Pretentious edgy poetry magic aside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1101759#post1101759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignore the fluff and 100+ books published. Take the core concept of each Covenant (pragmatic undead aristocracy, democratic and utilitarian vampires, bloodthirsty and monstrous pagans, self-righteous Judeo-Christian predators, transcendental order of Draconian undead) now, what can you do with these barebone concepts? Even &quot;elective democracy&quot; can be a shark pit of lethal politics, it doesn't necessarily have to be the feudalism of the Invictus that causes all the horror. Just look at the chaos today's democracy can create.</div> </div> </div> </div>No thanks? YMMV but the one thing that keep me away from Requiem for a long time was the core concept of the Covenant which were boring and unimaginative. Not many people give the Covenants book (Not the Secret of the covenant book, which is garbage) the credit it deserves as it really make them come alive and make sense.<br /> <br /> Undead aristocracy plain and simple lack sense if one doesn't understand the machinery that gives the Invictus and edge of the undead condition and society.<br /> <br /> USA university democracy/watered down anarchs brings the question of why would anyone join a clearly loosing side on the big scheme of things if one doesn't understand how ANY government that isn't the invictus (or any other covenant) is a Carthian by default.<br /> <br /> Monstrous pagans on its own bring the question who in the right mind would join them? Considering that going from average Joe to sacrifice people in blood rituals to the Goddess is a big step. If one didn't understand the variety and methods of recruitment and how they are basically defined by their opposition.<br /> <br /> And Judeo-Christian predators is a difficult sell to people who live in places in which religion is unimportant and just seem USA idea of Catholics faith to the extreme. Unless one reads how insidious they are and the key political alliance of Lay membership to the invictus can both boos the membership and ingratiate themselves to the other covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:12:55-07:00","id":1101799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1101780#post1101780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point was that Requiem can be as much of pant-on-the-head awesome-idiotic as it can be serious and exploring the vampire condition. Also, all that stuff i mentioned werent bloodlines disciplines. They came from the covenants books fluff, the gargoyles mechanics and the secret of the covenant/Core 2ed core merits. Pretentious edgy poetry magic aside.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No thanks? YMMV but the one thing that keep me away from Requiem for a long time was the core concept of the Covenant which were boring and unimaginative. Not many people give the Covenants book (Not the Secret of the covenant book, which is garbage) the credit it deserves as it really make them come alive and make sense.<br /> <br /> Undead aristocracy plain and simple lack sense if one doesn't understand the machinery that gives the Invictus and edge of the undead condition and society.<br /> <br /> USA university democracy/watered down anarchs brings the question of why would anyone join a clearly loosing side on the big scheme of things if one doesn't understand how ANY government that isn't the invictus (or any other covenant) is a Carthian by default.<br /> <br /> Monstrous pagans on its own bring the question who in the right mind would join them? Considering that going from average Joe to sacrifice people in blood rituals to the Goddess is a big step. If one didn't understand the variety and methods of recruitment and how they are basically defined by their opposition.<br /> <br /> And Judeo-Christian predators is a difficult sell to people who live in places in which religion is unimportant and just seem USA idea of Catholics faith to the extreme. Unless one reads how insidious they are and the key political alliance of Lay membership to the invictus can both boos the membership and ingratiate themselves to the other covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was not to take away the depth but to ignore all the fluff and super speshul disciplines and the like. We are on the same page anyway, now I see your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T00:45:41-07:00","id":1101881,"title":"","content":"All that fluff and speshul disciplines is part of of the published material, though, so ignoring it is no more right than including it in order to make a campaign based on the filmography of John Woo. And frankly, all the fighting styles in the core books of 2e give you all you need to do just that.<br /> <br /> The &quot;personal horror&quot; and &quot;realistic&quot; aspects are represented in a few mechanics, but mostly, it's how the game is marketed. You could do tragic personal stories about characters struggling with everyday problems and morality without ever leaving their neighbourhood in Shadowrun with no problems, but the game is marketed as &quot;take your team of misfits to missions to infiltrate worldwide corporations for clients who will try to stab you in the back for for THEIR worldwide corporation's sake.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, don't sweat the &quot;The game is about this and that&quot; side of things. There is a certain mood intended, sure, but the game is about what you want it to be about. Until it's played, it's just a book. One thing I love about the game is that for all it's talk of being about street level drama, the tools it gives you allow you to do pretty much anything you want with it. Plus, I don't see how personal horror is mutually exclusive with epic shit and kung fu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T01:50:46-07:00","id":1101887,"title":"","content":"In general there is no &quot;wrongbadfun&quot;. You want your vamp to mope and cry in the ocrner go for it. You want to him to use Animalism to command his ghouled sharks(that are also on fire)? I know I want to do that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T11:37:35-07:00","id":1102057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1101759#post1101759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just look at the chaos today's democracy can create.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, America is a republic. The electoral colleges are the ones who decide the next leaders. Theoretically, the people of America tell them who the vote for, but in 21 states, they don't have to listen to us. Meaning that your vote literally doesn't count for anything.<br /> <br /> But yeah, trying to climb the ranks of a society like that can still involve a hefty degree of kissing ass and social maneuvering so that when you finally do get in power, everybody believes that they actually want you there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ironically, the Circle of the Crone does offer the chance to play as an &quot;ass kicking vampire&quot; perspective, since they often tend to deify the vampiric existence. You could have a cult of mortals who wait on you hand and foot while you flaunt your power to foolish unbelievers. But going too far has <b>consequences</b>, which is what the personal horror is all about. Your actions carry emotional / social weight and you have to carry that weight for the rest of eternity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T16:43:41-07:00","id":1103324,"title":"","content":"As someone who plays Vampire but utterly detests the very idea of personal horror, allow me to weigh in on this. Do note that there is nothing wrong with personal horror in and of itself, but that it is not suited for my personal tastes. That is all.<br /> <br /> But to answer the question, despite what some people claim, there is NO &quot;Wrong Way&quot; to play Vampire: The Requiem, All the games I run and write are very much in the vein of badassery and heroism. My games are either &quot;Heroic Vampires defying the darkness&quot;, &quot;Dark Adventure in a modern setting&quot;, or alternately, &quot;Grand Theft Auto with fangs&quot;. I sometimes include political backstabbing, but angst and personal horror are explicitly not part of my style of game.<br /> <br /> The game is a toolkit, and people often forget that Requiem and the nWoD/CofD was initially designed as a toolkit to accommodate multiple styles of gameplay and narrative focus following the metaplot excesses of Masquerade (which some liked, but others did not). Unfortunately, personal horror was presented as the default theme, and while that in and of itself was not the issue, a lot of people interpreted the idea that the default theme was the only way to play the game when it was simply one valid option out of many equally valid options.<br /> <br /> Rule Zero exists for a reason and Requiem encourages it, even back in the 1e days (I myself prefer using 1e and making minor modifications instead of fooling around with 2e, but that's just my personal mechanics preference), so if you don't like something, then change it!<br /> <br /> Eat the chicken and throw away the bone, as the old saying goes.<br /> <br /> I run my games as dark adventure games, often with heroic PC's (even if they are vampires) with absolutely no angst or personal horror (action horror is present from time to time, though), and only as much political backstabbing as the players want. Others run their game differently and that is fine as well.<br /> <br /> It's your game, make it what you want it to be and ignore the haters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T17:34:57-07:00","id":1103667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1103324#post1103324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who plays Vampire but utterly detests the very idea of personal horror, allow me to weigh in on this. Do note that there is nothing wrong with personal horror in and of itself, but that it is not suited for my personal tastes. That is all.<br /> <br /> But to answer the question, despite what some people claim, there is NO &quot;Wrong Way&quot; to play Vampire: The Requiem, All the games I run and write are very much in the vein of badassery and heroism. My games are either &quot;Heroic Vampires defying the darkness&quot;, &quot;Dark Adventure in a modern setting&quot;, or alternately, &quot;Grand Theft Auto with fangs&quot;. I sometimes include political backstabbing, but angst and personal horror are explicitly not part of my style of game..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glad someone feels that way lol, I like the story and opportunity to go outside the limitations of video games - that to me is the running gag, the main bit that makes this all attractive. Not the munchkins, not the competition (although certainly some parts are fun, this sort of thing is hardly the sum of it's parts though)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T06:59:15-07:00","id":1103790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1103324#post1103324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who plays Vampire but utterly detests the very idea of personal horror, allow me to weigh in on this. Do note that there is nothing wrong with personal horror in and of itself, but that it is not suited for my personal tastes. That is all.<br /> <br /> But to answer the question, despite what some people claim, there is NO &quot;Wrong Way&quot; to play Vampire: The Requiem, All the games I run and write are very much in the vein of badassery and heroism. My games are either &quot;Heroic Vampires defying the darkness&quot;, &quot;Dark Adventure in a modern setting&quot;, or alternately, &quot;Grand Theft Auto with fangs&quot;. I sometimes include political backstabbing, but angst and personal horror are explicitly not part of my style of game.<br /> <br /> The game is a toolkit, and people often forget that Requiem and the nWoD/CofD was initially designed as a toolkit to accommodate multiple styles of gameplay and narrative focus following the metaplot excesses of Masquerade (which some liked, but others did not). Unfortunately, personal horror was presented as the default theme, and while that in and of itself was not the issue, a lot of people interpreted the idea that the default theme was the only way to play the game when it was simply one valid option out of many equally valid options.<br /> <br /> Rule Zero exists for a reason and Requiem encourages it, even back in the 1e days (I myself prefer using 1e and making minor modifications instead of fooling around with 2e, but that's just my personal mechanics preference), so if you don't like something, then change it!<br /> <br /> Eat the chicken and throw away the bone, as the old saying goes.<br /> <br /> I run my games as dark adventure games, often with heroic PC's (even if they are vampires) with absolutely no angst or personal horror (action horror is present from time to time, though), and only as much political backstabbing as the players want. Others run their game differently and that is fine as well.<br /> <br /> It's your game, make it what you want it to be and ignore the haters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all well and good, but if there isn't a consense around which kind of game to be played at the table, then there's not going to be fun for everyone involved. If someone doesn't wants to deal with constant PVP at the table, and gets unduly targeted by it, chances are they won't like it. Which is the OP's conundrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T16:25:47-07:00","id":1104008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1103790#post1103790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all well and good, but if there isn't a consense around which kind of game to be played at the table, then there's not going to be fun for everyone involved. If someone doesn't wants to deal with constant PVP at the table, and gets unduly targeted by it, chances are they won't like it. Which is the OP's conundrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite, and PVP can be a real pain in the ass and bring the experience down for everyone if they get attached to their characters (which if they've spent a lot of time making them will likely be the case)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T20:33:25-07:00","id":1104133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1100320-what-makes-this-game-fun?p=1103790#post1103790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all well and good, but if there isn't a consense around which kind of game to be played at the table, then there's not going to be fun for everyone involved. If someone doesn't wants to deal with constant PVP at the table, and gets unduly targeted by it, chances are they won't like it. Which is the OP's conundrum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always make sure to let my players know what kind of game I intend to run (especially given the rather prevalent misconception within the White Wolf/Onyx Path fandom that the default themes presented are somehow the only themes allowed). If they want a personal horror game, there's plenty of other options out there. Requiem games done the way I enjoy are comparatively much more rare and as such, I have taken it upon myself to be the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> So, I do understand the importance of player consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 06-15-2017, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}